num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Undistributed (excess) reportable income**\n- Excess reportable income (reportable income minus actual distributions) is **deemed distributed** on the fund distribution date, six months after the reporting period ends. You're taxed in the **UK tax year containing that date**, despite receiving no cash.\n- It's generally taxed as a **dividend**, but as **interest (savings income)** if the fund holds over 60% interest-bearing assets throughout the period (qualifying investments test).\n- It's **added to your CGT base cost**, avoiding double taxation on disposal.\n\n**Disposal gains**\n- Gains face **capital gains tax**, not income tax, at the current 18% and 24% rates. The £3,000 annual exempt amount and losses can offset gains.\n- Gain = proceeds minus cost, where cost includes reported excess income. This assumes reporting status throughout ownership.\n\nCheck each fund's annual report (fund website or HMRC's list) and report the figures on your Self Assessment return.","ttft_ms":1321,"type":"result","duration_ms":3664,"uuid":"24e12e91-0497-404a-881b-76d1fcb13827","ttft_stream_ms":501,"time_to_request_ms":69,"first_content_frame_ms":502,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
